  "query_preview": "..\nCurrently there is a cut off low in Sonora, Mexico that is \nspinning. There is just enough moisture around for a stray\nshower this afternoon, but chances remain minimal at less than\n15% in Cochise County, where it is closest to the low, but\ngenerally unfavored dynamics. This low is increasing the \nsurface easterly winds this afternoon into tomorrow as the low \ncontinues to linger. Winds will be at 12-20 mph and gusts to 30 \nmph. The low will begin to slowly open up and move eastward as \nhigh pressure begins to build behind it. This will keep the area\ndry, with only changes to sensible weather during with a \npassing shortwave Monday into Tuesday. \n\nEnsembles continue to show a low pressure system moving down the\nWest Coast and working it's way into Southeastern Arizona Friday\ninto Saturday and possibly another system behind that as well.\nThe NBM continues with general PoPs 20-30% across much of the\narea with rainfall totals less than 0.5 inches, but this will\nlikely change as we gain confidence in how much moisture can be\ntapped into and where dynamics can set up.",
